    {
      "id": "night",
      "kind": "run",
      "why": "the night of the place demo/walk stands in, put at the sun's own depth rather than at a wall-clock hour: 23:00 UTC on 6 August puts the sun 21.14 deg under this horizon with the moon 11.36 deg over it (measured, `outshine scene sunElDeg` and `sim stand moonElDeg`), so it is past astronomical twilight and what is left in the frame is moonlight and whatever the world itself emits. cloudCover is 0 because a deck is the one thing that would hide that answer. The camera turns a full 360 deg over 120 frames and every frame is written: a light that switches on, a lamp that pops in at a range and a surface that only glows from one bearing are three different defects and a still shows none of them.",
      "fovDeg": 60,
      "stage": {
